From 8496eef77438ac22f245a715e78177b8329a94bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:32:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban delegation: judge built-child overrides by
 provenance, admit the allocated route's own extra_body

Review of PR #4048 at 1b4afbaf3293 (t_59ae72a4aa530f45) found a regression this PR introduced (B1):
`_build_children` re-ran `check_request_overrides` on the built child's whole `request_overrides`.
Construction merges the allocator-selected custom route's own `custom_providers[].extra_body` into that
mapping (`agent_init._merge_custom_provider_extra_body`), so a valid `class:deep` delegation from a Kanban
worker was refused whenever the allocator landed on a custom route whose operator config carries
`provider` / `models` / `route` / `model` in `extra_body`. On base that delegation works.

Why it happened: the post-construction check treated everything in the final mapping as caller authority.
Operator route config and delegation overrides were only told apart by key name, not by where they came from.

Fix: `kanban_delegation_policy.check_built_child(child, tier)` judges each source on its own record.
- The tier overlay and the caller's body captured before the merge (`_caller_extra_body`) refuse any routing
  key, whether or not its value equals the route config. The pre-construction checks are unchanged, so a
  caller overlay is still refused before a child is built.
- A routing key in the final `extra_body` is admitted only when the child's own route config, re-read from
  `custom_providers` for its concrete provider/model/endpoint, holds the same key with the same value.
- Everything else in the final mapping gets the full check, so a key added or replaced after the merge
  still refuses. Nothing is removed from what the child sends.

Tests (tests/tools/test_kanban_delegation_component79.py), through real `_routes_for` + `_build_children`
+ `AIAgent` unless marked unit:
- route extra_body with provider/models/route, and with model: RED on 1b4afbaf3293 (the reviewer's
  refusal text), GREEN here; the child's request_overrides equal the route config.
- controls, green before and after: route extra_body service_tier only; native anthropic route.
- tier overlay carrying routing keys equal to the route config (spoof), same key equal, same key different,
  top-level model: child is built, refused before launch and closed.
- caller overlay equal to the route config: refused at `_routes_for`, nothing constructed.
- unit, `check_built_child`: caller-owned equal value, case variant, replaced value, added key, no trusted
  route, another provider's config, top-level / extra_query / header keys, malformed shapes.

Not covered here: header/query credential names beyond Authorization, x-api-key, api-key and host are not
refused (operator config only; unchanged by this commit). Auxiliary, MoA, curator, side-question, plugin and
external delegation paths, `register_root` against a live worker process, and macOS/Windows stay unproven.

Card: t_b76fc0ced1eeacb2
